<title>UK: NIB sets 400 million Danish crown step-up bond.</title>
<headline>NIB sets 400 million Danish crown step-up bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Den Danske Bank and Generale Bank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NORDIC INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    400 MLN DKR   COUPON    *ZERO	MATURITY    30 DEC.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STEP-UP   ISS PRICE  101.66    PAY DATE    17.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES     *ZERO COUPON TO 1999 THEN &quot;JUMPS-UP' TO 10.25 PCT</p>
<p>		THEREAFTER.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
